// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`meili config sync-with-cloud > prints its help without any network call 1`] = `
"Set the cloudId of the config file entries whose URL is a Meilisearch Cloud project the token sees. Never writes a key, never adds or removes an entry. Prints what changed.

USAGE
  $ meili config sync-with-cloud [-o <mode>] [--debug] [--management-token <pat>]
    [--management-url <url>] [--team-id <id>]

FLAGS
  -o, --output=<mode>           json (default): one document, the API body as it
                                is, indented in a terminal, compact when piped.
                                ndjson: one item per line, list commands only,
                                streams with --all.
      --debug                   Print every HTTP request and response on stderr,
                                secrets redacted.
      --management-token=<pat>  Management API personal access token.
      --management-url=<url>    Management API base URL. Default
                                https://api.meilisearch.com.
      --team-id=<id>            Only the projects of this team; missing entries
                                are then not reported.

DESCRIPTION
  Set the cloudId of the config file entries whose URL is a Meilisearch Cloud
  project the token sees. Never writes a key, never adds or removes an entry.
  Prints what changed.

  The file holds API keys and decides where every later command goes, for every
  process that reads it: an agent runs this only when the human asked for it
  explicitly.

EXAMPLES
  $ meili config sync-with-cloud

  $ meili config sync-with-cloud --team-id 12

  $ meili config sync-with-cloud --output json

"
`;
